course: dictionary
lesson: 5550
title: Same spelling, different meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the same spelling can even mean different things. Lei has two meanings in this dictionary entry, and it can also be a person's name. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context.
explain: «In Chinese names the family name comes first: in "Wang Lei", Wang is the surname.» Here Lei is a person's name, not a flower or money. The capital letter, and the name Wang next to it, are clues that Lei is a name for a person.
explain: A lei is a Hawaiian garland or necklace made of flowers, leaves, shells or feathers. People give a lei as a sign of welcome, love or celebration. In a money sum about Romania or Moldova, lei is the currency, so the meaning is money, not a necklace.
fact: A lei is a Hawaiian garland or necklace made of flowers, leaves, shells or feathers.
fact: A lei is given as a sign of welcome, love or celebration.
fact: Lei is also the plural of «leu», the money of Romania and Moldova: one leu, ten lei.
fact: A capital letter and a name like «Wang Lei» can show that Lei is a person's name.
fact: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «She put a flower lei around my neck at the airport.» What is a lei here? | *A Hawaiian garland of flowers | A kind of shell | A person's name | A type of Romanian money
exercise: «The shop sold a bread roll for five lei.» What does lei mean here? | *Money of Romania and Moldova | A person's name | A feather hat | A flower garland
exercise: In «Wang Lei», what is Lei? | A necklace of shells | A flower garland | *A person's name | Money
test: Which word is the plural of «leu», the money? | leu's | *lei | leus | levs
test: What is a lei in Hawaii? | A road sign | *A garland or necklace of flowers, leaves, shells or feathers | A coin | A kind of bread
exam: Ella says, «I got a lei at the airport, and I have ten lei in my pocket from Bucharest.» Which lei is the flower garland? | Both are flower garlands | The second lei | Neither is a flower garland | *The first lei
